<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/Meadow-Grove-Fields.jpg" alt="The back fields at Meadow Grove Farm" width="450" height="357" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Meadow Grove Fields (plein air). 11x14, oil on linen panel. 2015</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Meadow Grove Farm in Upperville, VA is one of my favorite paint-out locations: lot of distant views across the fields, animals in abundance, a variety of scenery, trees singular and clustered, and the ever-present Blue Ridge. &nbsp;In short, a location that seems to fit my eye very well.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Today I set up behind the main house where I had a view across a field full of sheep. &nbsp;As usual, this is a composed image: I edited out fences, moved sheep, trees and even the mountain to create the scene that I wanted.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I was assisted by Flower the pot bellied pig, who helped herself to a few of my peanut butter crackers.</p>